  "notes": "SYNTHETIC control fixture (Borrower A). Invented entities only. This is the clean-PASS baseline that proves the kernel does not cry breach at everything: every covenant passes with comfortable headroom, the certificate matches the recompute exactly, there are no add-back games (the only add-back is allowed non-cash D&A), and the field map is stable across both certificates so no schema drift is detected. Arithmetic (GBP millions): EBITDA build = operating_profit + allowed D&A add-back; Q4-2025 40.0+8.0=48.0, Q1-2026 42.0+8.0=50.0. Net debt = term_loan + revolver_drawn - cash; Q4-2025 120.0+0.0-24.0=96.0, Q1-2026 118.0+0.0-28.0=90.0. Leverage = total_net_debt / consolidated_ebitda; Q4-2025 96.0/48.0=2.00x, Q1-2026 90.0/50.0=1.80x; ceiling 3.50x. Interest cover = consolidated_ebitda / net_finance_charges; Q4-2025 48.0/12.0=4.00x, Q1-2026 50.0/12.5=4.00x; floor 2.50x. Leverage improves 2.00x -> 1.80x, so watch_rule.deteriorating_periods (=3) never trips: definitively PASS, not WATCH. field_map_fingerprint algorithm: sha256 of ('\\n'.join(sorted('key:raw_name')) + '\\n#UNMAPPED#\\n' + '\\n'.join(sorted(unmapped_raw_names))). document.fingerprint.value = sha256('SYNTHETIC::' + doc_id + '::' + title + '::' + doc_date). expected_assessment[] is a test oracle only and must not be read by assess()."
